# Git's built-in `markdown` userdiff driver supplies an xfuncname, so hunk
# headers name the enclosing heading — `@@ -4,3 +4,3 @@ ## Pre-merge` instead of
# a bare line range. In a repo whose product is prose that is the difference
# between knowing which section a hunk lands in and not.
#
# It does NOT supply a wordRegex. `git diff --word-diff` — the thing that makes
# a paragraph edit legible here — is a display flag that needs no attribute, and
# its output is byte-identical with and without this line. See CLAUDE.md
# § Local dev setup, and scripts/test-markdown-diff-attribute.sh, which pins
# both halves of that claim against the installed git rather than restating it.
*.md diff=markdown
